#[

    File and Path Utilities Example

    This example demonstrates the usage of file
    and path utilities which provide functions 
    for common file and path operations such as 
    creating, reading, writing, appending, and 
    deleting files, as well as creating 
    directories, normalizing paths, and more.

    P.S.: It doesn't need to be this complicated
    just took me several days to figure out the 
    ffi -> dragonstone for io file handling 
    through crystal so i didn't have to create 
    the whole system. But ended up doing it 
    anyway, so here it is.
    
]#

#[

    This is the file and path utilities example, which is
    using the file and path utilities from the standard 
    library. This is depreciated in favor of using the
    file and path utilities directly from the system 
    library, which does not require imports and is more
    efficient.

    !# This will be removed in a future release, so it's
    !# recommended to switch to using the it from the
    !# system library directly.
    
]#

